ntfs-3g (ntfs-macos) patch 0013: ntfs_inode_sync_file_name() reads the reparse tag only from a complete resident value

Rationale (T-M3-25, ADR-026, finding F6, found in the review of patches 0010 to 0012, tests/fuzz/TRIAGE.md):
in NTFS-3G 2026.9.28, libntfs-3g/inode.c ntfs_inode_sync_file_name() (lines 815 to 822) looks up the
$REPARSE_POINT attribute of an inode whose standard information has FILE_ATTR_REPARSE_POINT and reads
rpp->reparse_tag at ctx->attr + le16_to_cpu(ctx->attr->value_offset) (4 bytes), with no test that the
attribute is resident and none of its length. ntfs_attr_inconsistent() has no AT_REPARSE_POINT case, and its
value_offset test is skipped when value_length is 0, so a crafted attribute reaches this read:
  - a non-resident $REPARSE_POINT: the "value_offset" field overlaps the non-resident header (it is not a
    value offset), so the read is at an arbitrary offset of up to 64 KiB from the attribute, past the end of
    the MFT record buffer;
  - a resident one with value_length 0 to 3: the read takes bytes that are not part of the value.
The function runs from ntfs_inode_sync() (line 977) when the inode has the file-name-dirty flag, so only on
read-write mounts. The value read is stored as reparse_point_tag (line 895) into the index entries of the
file's names in their directories.
Change (libntfs-3g/inode.c, one hunk): the tag is read only when !ctx->attr->non_resident and
le32_to_cpu(ctx->attr->value_length) >= sizeof(REPARSE_POINT); otherwise reparse_tag stays 0, the behaviour for
a file without reparse data.
Scope: library-wide and cross-platform (no __APPLE__ guard). It only adds a rejection of a malformed on-disk
attribute; a complete resident reparse attribute takes the same path as before.
Upstream status: not yet reported; draft report in build/upstream-reports/05-security-inode-sync-reparse.md;
carried per ADR-026.
Test: none of the replays reaches it (the harness mounts read-only; the sync path needs a read-write mount and a
crafted image with a reparse attribute that is non-resident or empty). Found by reading the code; no
reproducer was built. Covered only by the I-* integration cases and the probe and volmark suites not regressing.

--- a/libntfs-3g/inode.c
+++ b/libntfs-3g/inode.c
@@ -816,9 +816,18 @@
 	if (ni->flags & FILE_ATTR_REPARSE_POINT) {
 		if (!ntfs_attr_lookup(AT_REPARSE_POINT, NULL,
 				0, CASE_SENSITIVE, 0, NULL, 0, ctx)) {
-			rpp = (REPARSE_POINT*)((u8 *)ctx->attr +
+			/*
+			 * ntfs-macos 0013 : the tag is read only from a
+			 * resident value of at least the header size,
+			 * otherwise the file is handled as a non reparse one
+			 */
+			if (!ctx->attr->non_resident
+			    && (le32_to_cpu(ctx->attr->value_length)
+				>= sizeof(REPARSE_POINT))) {
+				rpp = (REPARSE_POINT*)((u8 *)ctx->attr +
 					le16_to_cpu(ctx->attr->value_offset));
-			reparse_tag = rpp->reparse_tag;
+				reparse_tag = rpp->reparse_tag;
+			}
 		}
 		ntfs_attr_reinit_search_ctx(ctx);
 	}
